    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What battery standard does Saudi Arabia use for trucks?</h3>
      <p>Saudi Arabia runs a mixed Japanese and European commercial fleet, so JIS N-series batteries (N150/N200, models 145G51/190H52) and DIN/EN batteries (DIN88/DIN100, models 58827/60038) are both used. The battery follows the vehicle, not the country — confirm group size, terminal layout and voltage against the truck.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Why does Saudi heat shorten truck battery life?</h3>
      <p>High ambient temperatures accelerate the chemical ageing of lead-acid plates and increase electrolyte water loss in flooded batteries. The result is faster self-discharge and a shorter service life than in temperate climates, so thick-plate construction and disciplined electrolyte care matter.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What certification does a battery need to enter Saudi Arabia?</h3>
      <p>Saudi Arabia requires SASO conformity assessment through the SABER platform, with a Product Certificate of Conformity (PCoC) and Shipment Certificate (SCoC). Gulf-wide, the G-Mark (Gulf Technical Regulation for Low Voltage Electrical Equipment) applies. Confirm the current scheme with your importer before shipping.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Do you supply batteries to Saudi Arabia?</h3>
      <p>Yes. DINWEYS exports JIS N150/N200 and DIN88/DIN100 heavy-duty batteries to Saudi distributors through Jeddah Islamic Port and King Abdulaziz Port Dammam, with batch CCA test data and full shipping documentation on every delivery.</p>
    </div>

